  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a rectangular fence with length LLL and width WWW.\n\nThe fence has **four sides**, and the total length of the fence is:\n2×(L+W)2 \\times (L + W)2×(L+W).\n\nYou have **exactly enough paint** to paint the entire fence using **three colors**: Red, Green, and Blue.\n\nLet the total available paint of each color be RRR, GGG, and BBB respectively, then:\nR+G+B=2×(L+W)R + G + B = 2 \\times (L + W)R+G+B=2×(L+W).\n\nEach unit of paint can cover one unit length of the fence.\n\nPainting Cost:\n\n\nEach side of the rectangle must be painted completely.\nA side may be painted using **one or more colors**.\nThe **cost of painting a side** is equal to the **number of distinct colors used on that side**.\nDetermine the **minimum total cost** required to paint the entire fence.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line containing five space-separated integers L,W,R,G,BL, W, R, G, BL,W,R,G,B - denoting the length and width of the rectangle, and total available paint for each color respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer — the **minimum total painting cost**.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤L,W≤1091 \\leq L, W \\leq 10^91≤L,W≤109",
      "1≤R,G,B≤1091 \\leq R, G, B \\leq 10^91≤R,G,B≤109",
      "R+G+B=2×(L+W)R + G + B = 2 \\times (L + W)R+G+B=2×(L+W)"
    ],
